      9-5.3  ByPass Idle Time
      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
      This is to bypass the node's idle timeout setting that kicks users 
      off the bbs if they don't do anything in so many minutes.  
      
      This setting can be set higher or lower than the node's setting to
      kick certain users off sooner or let them stay on longer than they
      would of normally.  leave this set to zero if you want the user to
      be kicked with the node's idle timeout setting.

      Keep in mind a long distance caller when adjusting this.  If you set
      a user higher than normal that is calling long distance and they walk
      away from their machine, they will stay on longer before being kicked.
      This will give them a higher phone bill for being on longer, so just  
      think about it before you set this setting.

