                APPENDIX F - SModem Bi-Directional Protocol
 __________________________________________________________________________
 __________________________________________________________________________

 SModem is a bi-directional protocol used to transfer files to and from a 
 bbs as the same time and allows for chating with the sysop while you are
 transfering to and from the bbs.

 o SModem should be placed in your C: directory.

 o Smodem is an external protocol so many things are not possible like with
   other protocols in Tempest.  I will attempt to get the source to smodem
   so I can eliminate all the problems and implement all the cool options
   Tempest offers.

   - Background upload processing is not possible for uploads with smodem.

   - Can not send any commands from the server to any node that is currenlty
     using smodem.

   - SModem will open its own screens/windows for every node using smodem.

   - SModem currently does not ever timeout if a user starts smodem.  It
     will abort if the user holds ctrl-x or drops carrier however.

